    "final_cot": "Image description: The attached figure shows a large triangle ADC, with A at the top, D at the lower left, and C at the lower right. Point E is on side AD, and point B is on side AC. Segment EB crosses the triangle, and EB and the base DC both have the same arrow markings, indicating EB ∥ DC. The left side is labeled AD = 8, and ED = 5, so AE = 8 - 5 = 3. On the right side, AB is labeled x + 2, and BC is labeled 6, so AC = AB + BC = (x + 2) + 6 = x + 8. Reasoning: Because EB ∥ DC, triangle AEB and triangle ADC are similar. Corresponding sides are proportional: AB/AC = AE/AD. Therefore (x + 2)/(x + 8) = 3/8. Cross-multiplying gives 8(x + 2) = 3(x + 8), that is, 8x + 16 = 3x + 24, 5x = 8, so x = 1.6. Thus AC = x + 8 = 1.6 + 8 = 9.6.",
